    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "YieldBlox suffered a $10M loss on February 22, 2026, after an attacker manipulated a thinly traded Stellar DEX oracle price for USTRY/USDC, inflating collateral value and draining USDC and XLM from a Blend V2 lending pool. The lending pool operator configured its oracle to source USTRY prices from a near-zero-volume SDEX market, enabling price manipulation by a single abnormal trade. There were no liquidity/deviation checks or circuit breakers at the protocol or oracle-adapter layer."
